[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/pulls/1254","id":1789474099,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBMdeZM5qqTUz","html_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/1254","diff_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/1254.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/1254.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/issues/1254","number":1254,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Create a new input syntax for function.","user":{"login":"DavidFangWJ","id":34878339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODc4MzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34878339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ","html_url":"https://github.com/DavidFangWJ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Motivation\r\nAdd a more compact syntax to function, such that\r\n```\r\nlet f(x : A, y: B) = e\r\n```\r\nshould behave the same as below:\r\n```\r\nlet f : (A, B) = fun (x, y) -> e\r\n```\r\nThis new function syntax is more analogous to other programming languages with strong data types, and is therefore easier to learn.\r\n\r\n### Implementation Details\r\nAccording to the current structure, there following files are modified.\r\n- For `Info.re`, a new field `rewrite_id` is introduced, which registers the correspondence between the rewritten `Exp.t` and the original one.\r\n- For `StaticsBase.re`, `check_annotated_function` is introduced to check whether the function is in the new specified syntax, passed as `Let(Ap, ...)`.\r\n- For `Statics.re` and `Elaborator.re`, additional code are introduced to process the new syntax.\r\n- For `ExplainThis.re` and `AppPat.re`, additional explanation categories are introduced.","created_at":"2024-03-25T13:47:04Z","updated_at":"2026-04-23T15:28:57Z","closed_at":"2026-04-23T15:27:57Z","merged_at":"2026-04-23T15:27:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"4c949a18ade0710687c7ff00231131f3cb20a06c","assignees":[{"login":"DavidFangWJ","id":34878339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODc4MzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34878339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ","html_url":"https://github.com/DavidFangWJ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dm0n3y","id":8718124,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTgxMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8718124?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm0n3y","html_url":"https://github.com/dm0n3y","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm0n3y/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm0n3y/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.